1
00:04:21,818 --> 00:04:27,818
Just one man can make a difference.

2
00:08:43,636 --> 00:08:49,636
Mad Max 2 is a adventure, action, thriller film directed by George Miller.

3
00:13:05,454 --> 00:13:11,454
Max Rockatansky returns as the heroic loner who drives the dusty roads of a
postapocalyptic Australian Outback in an unending search for gasoline.

4
00:17:27,272 --> 00:17:33,272
Arrayed against him and the other scraggly defendants of a fuel-depot encampment are the bizarre warriors commanded by
the charismatic Lord Humungus, a violent leader whose scruples are as barren as the surrounding landscape.

5
00:21:49,090 --> 00:21:55,090
Max Rockatansky, played by Mel Gibson.

6
00:26:10,909 --> 00:26:16,909
The Gyro Captain, played by Bruce Spence.

7
00:30:32,727 --> 00:30:38,727
Pappagallo, played by Michael Preston.

8
00:34:54,545 --> 00:35:00,545
The Toadie, played by Max Phipps.

9
00:39:16,363 --> 00:39:22,363
Wez, played by Vernon Wells.

10
00:43:38,181 --> 00:43:44,181
The Humungus, played by Kjell Nilsson.

11
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Mad Max 2 (released as The Road Warrior in the United States) is a 1981 Australian post-apocalyptic dystopian
action film directed by George Miller, who co-wrote it with Terry Hayes and Brian Hannant.

12
00:52:21,818 --> 00:52:27,818
It is the sequel to Mad Max (1979) and the second
installment in the Mad Max franchise.

13
00:56:43,636 --> 00:56:49,636
The film stars Mel Gibson reprising his role as "Mad Max" Rockatansky and follows a hardened man who
helps a community of settlers to defend themselves against a roving band of marauders.

14
01:01:05,454 --> 01:01:11,454
Filming took place in locations around Broken Hill,
in the Outback of New South Wales.

15
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
Mad Max 2 was released in Australia on 24 December 1981 to widespread critical acclaim; praise was given to Gibson's performance, the musical score,
cinematography, action sequences and costume design, with its sparing use of dialogue in particular being unprecedented for an action film.

16
01:09:49,090 --> 01:09:55,090
It was also a box office success, and the film's post-apocalyptic and punk
aesthetics helped popularise the genre in film and fiction writing.

17
01:14:10,909 --> 01:14:16,909
At the 10th Saturn Awards, the film won Best International Film and was nominated for five more awards: Best Director, Best
Actor for Gibson, Best Supporting Actor for Bruce Spence, Best Writing, and Best Costumes for Norma Moriceau.

18
01:18:32,727 --> 01:18:38,727
Mad Max 2 is widely hailed as both one of the greatest action films of all time and one of the greatest sequels ever
made, and fan clubs for the film and "road warrior"-themed activities continue into the 21st century.

19
01:22:54,545 --> 01:23:00,545
The film was followed by Mad Max Beyond Thunderdome in 1985.

20
01:27:16,363 --> 01:27:22,363
The film explores themes of mask, australia, chase, explosive, dystopia.

21
01:31:38,181 --> 01:31:44,181
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
